{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgp85C6hM5cebbmgJH4Po", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I added `parse_kv` as the `kvparse` feature under `src/shop/ext/`, with tests, and the full suite passes (10 tests).\n\n**Files**\n- `src/shop/ext/__init__.py`: new package. It did not exist, so I created it per CLAUDE.md.\n- `src/shop/ext/kvparse.py`: `parse_kv(line)`. Its docstring includes `Ticket: PAY-4102`.\n- `tests/test_kvparse_cases.py`: tests for the `_cases` naming rule. `tests/` did not exist, so I created it.\n- `CHANGELOG.md`: added `- PAY-4102: kvparse: add parse_kv for 'a=1;b=2' style text` under `## Unreleased`.\n\n**Behavior**\n- Splits on `;`, then strips each segment.\n- Skips empty and whitespace-only segments.\n- Splits each segment on the first `=` only, so `token=x=y` gives `\"x=y\"`.\n- Strips keys and values; a later duplicate key overwrites an earlier one.\n- Raises `ValueError` for a non-empty segment with no `=`.\n- Uses no `re` and no `os.path`.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- An empty key such as `=1` is kept as `\"\"` rather than rejected, because the spec did not cover it. Say if you want it to raise.\n- Empty values such as `a=` are allowed and return `\"\"`.\n\n**Environment note**\n- `python` is not on the PATH here, and the system Python refuses pip installs. I ran tests in a venv at `/tmp/pr2-venv`, outside the repo.\n- The repo is not under git, so I did not commit anything."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 291, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 291}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f0